    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "vacy protection across computer science, control engineering, and communication technology. Multiple types of research have been illustrated for distributed NE seeking with DP method [17]–[20]. A privacy-preserving distributed algorithm for seeking the NE was designed in [17] for aggregative games and [18] focused on quadratic network games. [19] extended privacy-preserving mechanisms for NE seeking to directed graph. Considering coupling constraints, [20] proposed a GNE seeking strategy for multi-cluster games. Though [21] investigated GNE seeking with privacy preservation, information exchange efﬁciency was not considered. Privacy and communication efﬁciency are seldom explored together in distributed GNE seeking for aggregative games though it is of great interest."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 6,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 48.96, 522.588, 300.198, 567.494 ],
    "font" : "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "The motivation of this paper is to study aggregative games with coupling constraints and to design an efﬁcient distributed algorithm to seek GNE of the games. The principal contributions of this paper can be outlined as follows:"
  }, {
    "type" : "list",
    "pdfua_tag" : "L",
    "id" : 7,
    "level" : "1",
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 58.92, 330.467, 300.421, 506.774 ],
    "numbering style" : "arabic numbers",
    "number of list items" : 3,
    "list items" : [ {
      "type" : "list item",
      "pdfua_tag" : "LI",
      "page number" : 1,
      "bounding box" : [ 58.92, 449.988, 300.181, 506.774 ],
      "font" : "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
      "font size" : 9.963,
      "text color" : "[0.0]",
      "content" : "1) We provide a novel communication-efﬁcient distributed GNE seeking algorithm (Algorithm 1), combining an event-triggered mechanism to decrease transmission rounds and a stochastic compressor to minimize transmitted bits.",
      "kids" : [ ]
    }, {
      "type" : "list item",
      "pdfua_tag" : "LI",
      "page number" : 1,
      "bounding box" : [ 58.92, 378.228, 300.421, 447.014 ],
      "font" : "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
      "font size" : 9.963,
      "text color" : "[0.0]",
      "content" : "2) Besides achieving efﬁcient communication, our algorithm ensures convergence to exact GNE by developing precise step size conditions (Theorem 1). In contrast to existing GNE seeking works ensuring accuracy [21], our proposed algorithm further reduces the communication cost.",
      "kids" : [ ]
    }, {
      "type" : "list item",
      "pdfua_tag" : "LI",
      "page number" : 1,
      "bounding box" : [ 58.92, 330.467, 300.331, 375.871 ],
      "font" : "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
      "font size" : 9.963,
      "text color" : "[0.0]",
      "content" : "3) We show that (0,δ)-differential privacy is achieved under a stochastic compressor (Theorem 2). Particularly, the algorithm guarantees asymptotic convergence to the GNE and privacy protection simultaneously.",
      "kids" : [ ]
    } ]
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 8,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 48.96, 233.867, 300.421, 314.654 ],
    "font" : "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "The organization of this paper is as follows: Section II presents the fundamental concepts and establishes the formulation for the problem. Section III provides an event-triggered and compressed distributed GNE seeking algorithm with an analysis of convergence and privacy. Section IV provides simulation examples to conﬁrm the obtained results, and Section V concludes the paper."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 9,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 48.959, 72.423, 300.369, 227.829 ],
